Z||000004||Tom88gt||05-24-2000||01:48 PM||||Check out Kelly's Blue book or similar publication.  Factor in the mileage.  Should put you in the ball park.  Your mileage is really low but it shouldn't increase the value by more than 50%.  <P>Don't use NADA Consumer Retail Edition.  A total crock of $hit.  Keeps used car dealers happy by allowing them to rip of the public.  You can get the NADA Dealers/Trade Edition book but only by subscription, $100/year I think.<P>I haven't looked it up but I would guess an 86 V-6 to be around $2000, so I'm guessing about $3000 for yours.  Remember, Fieros have been severly devalued due to the undesserved bad reputation they have.  Your benefit when buying, your loss when selling.  <P>Keep the car.  You can't find and average '86 and restore it to 25,000 mile condition for twice the cost.  Well maybe you can but you will never get your  $6000 back if you sell it.||||reg||1
